  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "An owner positioning a hotel as **upper-upscale** in Mexico should primarily consider brands such as **Hyatt Regency, InterContinental, Westin, Sheraton, Le Méridien, Renaissance, Wyndham Grand, Kimpton, Hyatt Centric, Tempo, and Moxy**. Those brands are identified in the source as upper-upscale options or as upper-upscale-adjacent contemporary brands, with some geared more toward business, resort, or lifestyle positioning.[1]\n\nIf the property is being positioned more as a **traditional upper-upscale** hotel, the source specifically highlights **InterContinental Hotels & Resorts, Hyatt Regency, Wyndham Grand, Westin, Sheraton, Le Méridien, Renaissance, Hotel Indigo, and Alila**.[1] For a more **modern or lifestyle** upper-upscale positioning, it points to **Hyatt Centric, Moxy, Tempo, and Kimpton**.[1]\n\nFor Mexico specifically, owners commonly also evaluate **Camino Real** and **Quinta Real** within the broader upscale-to-luxury spectrum, though the source places **Real Inn** in upper midscale rather than upper-upscale.[2]\n\nA practical shortlist for Mexico would therefore include:\n- **Hyatt Regency**\n- **InterContinental**\n- **Westin**\n- **Sheraton**\n- **Le Méridien**\n- **Renaissance**\n- **Wyndham Grand**\n- **Kimpton**\n- **Hyatt Centric**\n- **Tempo**\n- **Moxy**\n- **Hotel Indigo**\n- **Alila**[1]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the best **upper-upscale brands with a strong Mexico presence** versus those that are strong globally but less common in Mexico.",
